ries being monitored for a brand, including which are currently enabled and which were auto-generated as baselines.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Creates a new brand for AI Visibility monitoring, triggering an initial analysis automatically. Ask which AI platforms to track. Supported platforms: %s. Selecting more than one requires the Expert plan; other plans may choose only one.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Language the brand should be analyzed in (e.g. "US English", "French"). Required; immutable after creation — ask the user which language to use.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Analysis refresh cadence. Defaults to the account plan\'s default when omitted.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'AI platforms to track. Supported: %s. Selecting more than one requires the Expert plan; otherwise choose exactly one. Do not assume a default — ask the user which platform(s) to use.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns the full normalized Rank Math settings snapshot: all four sections (general, titles, sitemap, instant_indexing), active module status, and auto-update state. Call this first in any AI configuration flow to understand what is already configured before making changes.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Return only these top-level sections. Omit to return the full snapshot.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get system status'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns a structured system health snapshot identical to Status & Tools → System Status in the admin: Rank Math version, plan, DB table health, Google token status, WordPress core info, server environment, and active plugins. Call this alongside get-settings at the start of any AI configuration flow to detect environment issues before making changes.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get llms.txt'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns whether the llms.txt file is enabled, its URL, and the current generated Markdown content.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether the llms.txt module is active.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The URL of the llms.txt file.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The generated llms.txt Markdown content. Empty when the module is disabled.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get robots.txt'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns the current robots.txt content managed by Rank Math.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The current robots.txt content: the real file contents when a physical robots.txt exists, otherwise the content Rank Math generates (custom override or computed default).'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether a physical robots.txt file exists in the site root.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether the site is set to be visible to search engines (Settings > Reading > Search engine visibility).'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set website identity'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates the site\'s Knowledge Graph identity used by Rank Math for schema and social markup: knowledge graph type (person/company), website name, alternate name, knowledge graph name, organization description, business type, and site URL override. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether the site represents a person or a company/organization.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The website name used in schema and social markup.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'An alternate name for the website.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The person or organization name used in the Knowledge Graph.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Description of the organization. Only used when knowledgegraph_type is "company".'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Schema.org business type slug (e.g. "Restaurant", "LegalService", "Organization"), spaces removed. Only used when knowledgegraph_type is "company". Call get-settings first or see the Local SEO business type list in WP Admin for valid values.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Site URL override used in Knowledge Graph markup.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set global SEO settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates site-wide SEO defaults: global robots meta directives, whether to noindex empty taxonomy archives, the title separator character, title capitalization, and the default Twitter card type. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Global robots meta directives applied site-wide (e.g. ["index"], ["noindex","nofollow"]).'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether to noindex taxonomy archives that have no posts assigned.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Character used to separate parts of the SEO title (e.g. "-", "|", "&mdash;"). A custom string is also accepted.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether to capitalize the first letter of every word in SEO titles.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Default Twitter card type used when sharing content.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set homepage SEO'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates the SEO title, meta description, and focus keyword for the site homepage. Automatically detects whether the homepage is a static page or a latest-posts feed and writes to the correct storage in each case. Call get-settings first to see current homepage values. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'SEO title for the homepage. Supports Rank Math title variables (e.g. %sitename%, %sep%, %sitedesc%). For static-page homepages, stored as post meta; for latest-posts homepages, stored in Titles & Meta settings.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Meta Description'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Meta description for the homepage. For static-page homepages, stored as post meta; for latest-posts homepages, stored in Titles & Meta settings.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Primary focus keyword for the homepage. Only applicable when the homepage is a static page — ignored for latest-posts homepages.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set link settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates site-wide link behavior: nofollow for external and image links, opening external links in a new tab, nofollow domain allow/exclude lists, category base stripping, and attachment page redirects. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Automatically add rel="nofollow" to external links in content.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Automatically add target="_blank" to external links in content.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Automatically add rel="nofollow" to links pointing to external image files.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Newline-separated list of domains to nofollow. If empty, nofollow applies to all external domains (when enabled). Only takes effect when nofollow_external_links or nofollow_image_links is also enabled — hidden in the UI otherwise.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Newline-separated list of domains to exclude from nofollow. Only takes effect when nofollow_external_links or nofollow_image_links is also enabled — hidden in the UI otherwise.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Remove /category/ from category archive URLs.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Redirect attachment page URLs to the post they appear in.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set module status'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Enables or disables Rank Math modules (e.g. sitemap, redirections, 404-monitor, rich-snippet). Only provided module slugs are changed; omitted modules keep their current state. Modules with unmet dependencies (e.g. Video Sitemap requires Sitemap and Schema) cannot be enabled until their dependencies are active or enabled in the same call. Modules whose external requirements are not met (e.g. WooCommerce module without the WooCommerce plugin active) cannot be enabled at all.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Map of module slug to desired active state. Call get-settings first to see the full list of registered module slugs and their current status.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set sitemap settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates XML sitemap settings: links per sitemap page, image inclusion, excluded post/term IDs, author archive inclusion, and per-post-type/per-taxonomy sitemap inclusion. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value. Requires the sitemap module to be active; enable it first with set-module-status if needed.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Include reference to images from the post content in sitemaps.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Include the Featured Image too, even if it does not appear directly in the post content. Only takes effect when include_images is also enabled.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Comma-separated post IDs to exclude from the sitemap. Applies to all post types.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Comma-separated term IDs to exclude from the sitemap. Applies to all taxonomies.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Include Authors in Sitemap'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Post Types'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Map of post type slug to whether it should be included in the XML sitemap. Call get-settings first to see registered post type sitemap status.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Taxonomies'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Map of taxonomy slug to whether it should be included in the XML sitemap.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set plugin preferences'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates Rank Math plugin-level preferences that are not part of a settings section. Currently supports toggling automatic plugin updates.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Enable Automatic Updates'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether WordPress should automatically install new Rank Math plugin updates.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set post type SEO settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates per-post-type SEO defaults: default title/description templates, default Schema type, default article type, custom robots meta, and whether to show SEO controls on the editor screen. Accepts a map keyed by post type slug; only provided post types and fields are changed.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Map of post type slug to its SEO settings. Call get-settings first to see registered post type slugs.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Single Title'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Default title tag for single pages of this post type. Supports Rank Math title variables.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Single Description'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Default meta description for single pages of this post type. Supports Rank Math variables.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Default Schema type slug for new posts of this type (e.g. "off", "article", "product", "event"). Call get-settings first or see the Schema Type list in WP Admin for valid values — the list varies per post type and active modules.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Default article schema sub-type. Only used when default_rich_snippet is "article".'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Custom Robots Meta'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether to use custom robots meta values for this post type instead of the Global Meta default.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Custom robots meta values for this post type. Only takes effect when custom_robots is enabled.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether to add SEO controls to the editor screen for posts of this type.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Set breadcrumb settings'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Updates breadcrumb display settings: enabling breadcrumbs, the separator, home link visibility/label/URL, a prefix before the trail, archive/search/404 label formats, ancestor category display, hiding the taxonomy name, removing the current post title, and showing the blog page. All fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current stored value.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Enable Breadcrumbs'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Enable the Breadcrumbs feature.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Character to display between breadcrumb links.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Show Home Link'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Show a link to the homepage at the start of the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Home Label'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Label used for the homepage link in the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Home Link'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'URL used for the homepage link in the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Text to show before the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Label format used for archive pages in the breadcrumb trail. Include a placeholder token for the archive title.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Label format used for search results pages in the breadcrumb trail. Include a placeholder token for the search query.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'404 Label'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Label used for the 404 error item in the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Hide the current post/page title from the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'If the category is a child category, show all ancestor categories in the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Hide the current taxonomy term name from the breadcrumb trail.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Show the blog page in the breadcrumb trail. Only applies when a static homepage is set.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns SEO scores and grades for posts. Before running, ask the user which posts they want to review: posts needing improvement (bad score), posts with no focus keyword, unscored posts, or simply the most recently modified posts. Use this to surface which posts need SEO attention without needing to know post IDs in advance.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Post type to filter by (e.g. "post", "page"). Defaults to all public post types.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Ask the user which posts they want to review before running this ability. Available options: "bad" (score ≤ 50, needs improvement), "good" (score 51–80, ok), "great" (score > 80), "empty-fk" (no focus keyword set), "unscored" (never analyzed). If the user does not specify, omit this parameter to return the most recently modified posts.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Gathers the raw content, metadata, and list of on-page SEO tests for a saved post so an AI agent can run Rank Math\'s full on-page analysis itself, since the scoring engine only runs client-side. Use tests_to_run and content together with kb_link (the scoring rubric for all 24 tests) to evaluate each test and produce a per-test score, status, and fix message.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Optional focus keyword to analyze against, overriding the post\'s saved focus keyword.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get sitemap status'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Returns whether the XML sitemap is enabled, the sitemap index URL, and the active sitemap types (post types, taxonomies, and the Local SEO sitemap, when active) with their URLs and estimated entry counts.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Whether the XML sitemap module is active.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The URL of the sitemap index file.'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'The active sitemap types, e.g. post types, taxonomies, and the Local SEO sitemap (PRO adds news/video when active).'=>['saveStringInDb'=>true,'cmp'=>['WordPress',3],'names'=>[],'urls'=>[]],'Get 404 log